Nope, nope.  Save files and bones files are completely separate.  You
can make and use _lots_ of save files during the course of a game, but
by definition, you can only make one bones file, but you can use several.

Confused?  Good.

A bones file is created with 1/3 chance from the level where you die,
after level 1-3 (before level 4, when you die you just die), only if you
don't already have a bones level for that level (or it clobbers the
existing one, I'm not sure).

It contains your ghost (or, on a multiple player system, _somebody's_
ghost, and when you come to that level, you have 1/3 of getting the
bones level instead of a normal level. so, if there are bones levels
solid from 4 to 21, then you might expect to get about six of them in
one game.

Besides the ghost, a nasty, slow, hard to hit monster with an attitude
problem and a gross lack of visibility, the level also contains all the
goodies the ghost was carrying, except that more likely they're baddies
instead of goodies.

If you're particular deity of good fortune is one of the more playful
types, several players (or you several times) may have died on that
level and left a ghost, so you can end up being pursued at the speed of
a racing glacier by half a dozen ghosts at once, plus all the monsters
that killed them, possibly weilding the named weapons they had, and etc.
Bones levels tend to get nasty _really_ fast, and don't seem to be
susceptible to the 1/3 chance of being created after they first exist;
second and subsequent ghosts seem to create them 1/1th of the time.

Just one of the many interesting ways to get killed in nethack.

